PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Core anatomy unchanged: distal paracentral a. (ACA) perfuses medial paracentral lobule (contralateral foot/leg) + narrow convexity crest strip (proximal arm/shoulder). Precise left “tip/round-over” lesion therefore hits ACA–MCA border zone.  
Round-1 split persists: 1,2,3,5 correctly map tip to greater right-arm sensory loss (A) via somatotopic gradient (foot more proximal/medial, arm at crest). 4,6,7 claim foot predominance (B) by arguing foot zone extends onto dorsal bank at round-over.  
Key unresolved: exact cortical width of foot vs. proximal-arm strip at crest. Laterality eliminates C/D; question isolates sensory cortex, eliminating E. No new motor-only arguments. My belief remains A (somatotopy favors arm at most distal tip).}

